RUN_STATUS {"status":"waiting","last":"S8 fix F-04 (note: tmp-f04.spec.ts deleted; AC-016-05; unanalysed failures)","result":"done","gate":"not passed (DoD-I-02: AC-018-01, EX-018-02, AC-003-08 and AC-001-04 fail on test defects awaiting D-53; INC-2 tests fail as expected)","next":"/verify","waiting":"D-53 (test changes for AC-018-01, EX-018-02, AC-003-08, AC-001-04; non-blocking for `/verify`)","log":"C:\\Users\\tanej\\Documents\\LAB\\tanej_sdd-workflow_contacts_v001\\02_output\\logs\\run\\050-fix.json","decisions":[{"id":"D-53","text":"## D-53: tests AC-018-01, EX-018-02, AC-003-08 and AC-001-04 cannot pass as written (proposed changes, need the developer)\n- Timestamp: 2026-11-10\n- Session: S8 fix F-04\n- Class: approval\n- Type: non-blocking for the session (it went on with the other findings); the three tests stay failing until answered\n- Trigger: the failures the note told to analyse; the app is right in each case, so no app change was made.\n  - AC-018-01: the test expects exactly one textbox in `main` on the first-visit sign-in screen (\"one e-mail field\"). In Playwright 1.55.1 a `type=password` input has the role textbox, and the sign-in screen must have e-mail and password (R-001-01), so it has two. Aria snapshot: `textbox \"E-pošta (obvezno)\"`, `textbox \"Geslo (obvezno)\"`.\n  - EX-018-02: the test clicks the `SL` button while the \"Create group\" dialog is open. The dialog is modal (Radix: everything outside is `aria-hidden` and inert), so the header switch is not reachable by role. A non-modal dialog would be an accessibility regression (focus trap).\n  - AC-003-08: `createAccount(IVAN, { verified: false })` creates the account through the emulator API, which issues no verification e-mail; the app sends one only at registration and on \"Send again\" (R-001-04, EX-001-06). `verifyEmail(IVAN.email)` then throws \"No verification e-mail for ivan@example.com\". It passes only when an earlier test left a code for the same address in the emulator (`resetStack` does not clear codes), hence \"flaky\".\n  - AC-001-04 (flaky, 1 pass in 4 runs, `out/logs/fix-f04b-run5.log`): after the CSP fix (D-54) the app signs in. The test clicks \"Add new account\" in the emulator popup right after the popup opens; when the click comes before the popup page has attached its handler it is lost and `Auto-generate user information` never appears (30 s timeout). A manual script that waits for the popup to load passes every time.\n- Options: (1) Approve test changes (proposed): AC-018-01 count the e-mail field only (`locator('input[type=email]')` toHaveCount(1)); EX-018-02 close the dialog (Escape) before the switch and assert the error text after submitting the duplicate again, or switch the language before opening the dialog; AC-001-04 `await popup.waitForLoadState('load')` before the first click; AC-003-08 click \"Send again\" before `verifyEmail`, or make `createAccount(..., { verified: false })` call `accounts:sendOobCode`. Update `docs/03_acceptance-manifest.sha256`. (2) Keep the tests and list them in the release notes. (3) Change the app (non-modal dialog, a language switch inside every dialog, a verification e-mail on every unverified sign-in): not recommended.\n- Human response: pending (answer with `/fix F-04 D-53: 1`)\n- Resolution: open\n- Overrides: none"}]}
